# Lines make check-serial (and tools/pi-run, live) must see on the Pi 5, in
# this order, as whole serial lines: rpi5b_2gb/usb-audio-loop-pi-test.system,
# the Pi 5 only. Each USB host PD runs its controller as
# usb-test's do, and the client starts; what is plugged in, on which port,
# differs by desk and is printed between these lines, not checked here - the
# run's log shows each side's devices, each stream's 10 s reports, and each
# recording made and played back; the person at the desk hears the tone and
# the recording. The run ends at its run length, 180 s (the ticker's last
# line). A missed interval, a stream not streamed or a speaker the client
# fed too little anywhere in the run fails it.
NOWAYOS: usb0: starting
NOWAYOS: usb0: controller identified
NOWAYOS: usb0: halted and reset
NOWAYOS: usb0: running: a No Op command came back through DMA
NOWAYOS: usb0: ready
NOWAYOS: usb1: starting
NOWAYOS: usb1: controller identified
NOWAYOS: usb1: halted and reset
NOWAYOS: usb1: running: a No Op command came back through DMA
NOWAYOS: usb1: ready
NOWAYOS: client: starting
NOWAYOS: client: ready: 2 USB host PDs to hear from
NOWAYOS: watchdog-stand-in: ticker: the run length is reached: no more ticks, so the watchdog services no more and the board resets

# Output that fails the run at once if it appears anywhere (substring match).
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!could not service
!not streamed
!missed so far
!sent too little
!no audio client
